<title>USA: West Virgina ruling favors tobacco companies.</title>
<headline>West Virgina ruling favors tobacco companies.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philip Morris USA  said on Friday that a West Virginia judge dismissed &quot;the essential claims&quot; of the state attorney general's Medicaid reimbursement lawsuit against tobacco companies.</p>
<p>Philip Morris said the ruling had implications for similar lawsuits in other states.</p>
<p>Circuit Judge Irene Berger on Thursday granted the tobacco industry's motion to dismiss 11 of the lawsuit's 14 counts, ruling that state agencies have no independent right to sue for personal injuries allegedly caused by smoking.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
